  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi attended the BRICS foreign ministers' meeting in New Delhi on May 15-17, where he described distrust as "the main obstacle to any diplomatic effort" and stated Iran "cannot trust the Americans at all." He confirmed that the enrichment question has reached "almost a deadlock" and acknowledged both sides agreed to "postpone" that issue to later stages of talks. The two-day BRICS ministerial ended without a joint statement after Iran and the UAE blocked consensus — Iran blaming UAE support for the US-Israel coalition, the UAE denying responsibility. Araghchi's statements were not preceded by any reported Khamenei green-light or briefing, consistent with Iran's pattern of letting the foreign ministry absorb public-diplomacy pressure while the supreme leader maintains strategic silence. → moved <span class="cite">N4</span>, <span class="cite">N7</span></p>

      <p>Iran's semi-official Fars News Agency published on May 13 a set of five preconditions Tehran requires before entering a new round of talks: end of hostilities on all fronts, lifting of sanctions, release of frozen assets, compensation for war damage, and US recognition of Iranian sovereignty over the Strait of Hormuz. None of these conditions has been met as of May 18. The five preconditions framing replaces Iran's earlier practice of conducting indirect back-channel talks while publicly maintaining ambiguity about terms — the publication of a specific list in a semi-official outlet represents a hardening of the stated floor. → moved <span class="cite">N4</span>, <span class="cite">N6</span>, <span class="cite">F6</span></p>

      <p>On the Israeli domestic track, Shas — the ultra-Orthodox Sephardic party holding 7 Knesset seats — confirmed on May 18 that it will vote in favor of the dissolution bill at the preliminary reading scheduled for Wednesday, May 20. Speaker Amir Ohana has maintained the May 20 date without scheduling any last-minute Haredi compromise session, though coalition sources described ongoing negotiations with Degel HaTorah over the yeshiva-draft framework. No court injunction against the vote was filed as of Monday morning. The full dissolution process requires four readings and the House Committee must then set a specific election date. → moved <span class="cite">N3</span></p>

      <p>Bloomberg's Hormuz Strait tracker published on May 17 showed daily transits at approximately 10 vessels, up from five the previous day, with the uptick driven by Iranian-linked incoming tankers — not by Western commercial resumption. Lloyd's List and the LMA confirmed war-risk premiums remain in the 1.5-3% of hull range. Maersk's one vehicle carrier that transited on May 6 under US military escort has not been followed by any scheduled commercial return. Project Freedom remains officially paused; no CENTCOM restart statement was issued during the May 16-18 window. → supports <span class="cite">F6</span> without move, moved <span class="cite">N6</span></p>

      <p>Trump's Middle East tour concluded on approximately May 16 with his departure from Abu Dhabi, where he received the Order of Zayed and signed an AI investment agreement worth approximately $1.4 trillion. No US-Iran bilateral session was scheduled or announced as a follow-on to the tour. Trump stated publicly that Iran had received a US nuclear proposal and that he wanted a deal, but no new channel or facilitator was named. Khamenei's April 30 written statement on protecting nuclear and missile capabilities as "national assets" — the most recent supreme-leader output — addressed Iran's general posture, not the specific negotiation track, and does not meet the resolution criteria for <span class="cite">N7</span>. → supports <span class="cite">N7</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
