      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (30%):</strong> Ceasefire collapses under the weight of Iran's five preconditions, US blockade continuation, and enrichment deadlock — the lowest-probability but structurally available path if Trump decides the "life support" language reflects genuine breakdown.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (48%):</strong> Most likely outcome: the 45-day Israel-Lebanon extension holds, the Iran-US ceasefire continues on a rolling basis, Hormuz remains frozen, talks restart intermittently but make no substantive progress on enrichment, and Israeli elections proceed on a domestic timeline independent of the regional war.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (22%):</strong> Requires both N4 (talks resume) and N7 (Khamenei publicly addresses the diplomatic track) to resolve YES, followed by a concrete enrichment compromise — a sequence requiring a Khamenei decision not yet in evidence.</p>
    </div>
