  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media coverage of the BRICS ministerial (May 15-17) followed a consistent framing: Araghchi's distrust language was reproduced prominently by IRNA and Press TV without the editorial qualifiers that Western outlets applied, presenting it as an authoritative government position rather than a negotiating posture. The parallel framing — that Iran "never wanted nuclear weapons" — ran simultaneously in Tasnim and IRNA, serving as a softener for domestic audiences anxious about war continuation while the hardline framing on distrust addressed the IRGC-aligned readership. → supports <span class="cite">N4</span> without move</p>

      <p>Fars News Agency's publication of the five preconditions on May 13 operated as the functional public record of Iran's negotiating floor. Fars is IRGC-adjacent; its publication of specific numbered conditions — as opposed to vaguer IRNA or Tasnim language — typically tracks coordination with the security establishment rather than a foreign ministry improvisation. The framing around Hormuz sovereignty (precondition five) ran prominently in Kayhan, which described the Strait as an "inalienable national territory" — reinforcing the hardliner position that any US escort operation is an act of occupation. The Kayhan framing did not use the specific rejection language (rad, mardud) that would resolve N-forecasts, keeping Iran's diplomatic options formally open. → supports <span class="cite">N6</span> without move, <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Mojtaba Khamenei's official channel (khamenei.ir) has published no statement addressing the negotiation track since the April 30 national-assets statement. State media have not reported any Araghchi-Khamenei briefing session following the BRICS trip. Mojtaba Khamenei communicates via written statements read on state television and published to khamenei.ir — he does not give Friday prayer addresses or make live public appearances. The 80-day silence on the specific diplomatic track continues, observable through the absence of new khamenei.ir content on the topic. → supports <span class="cite">N7</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

